senses.gloss:
--(also नैमिषालय s.v.) sacred to विष्णु; here शौनक and other sages performed a सत्र extending over a thousand years;
1: भा. I. 1. 4 and २१; III. २०. 7; VII. १४. ३१; Br. IV. 4. ४५.
visited by बलराम who was honoured by all except शूत Romahars2an2a; बलराम killed the शूत in anger thus committing brahmicide; then at the instance of the sages and as an expiation for the offence he killed Asura Balvala here;
2: भा. X. ७८. २०-32; ७९. 5.
revisited by बलराम who took part in the sacrifices;
3: Ib. X. ७९. ३०-32.
sages of, visited द्वारका.
4: Ib. X. ९०. २८. [6]. Br. I. 1. ३७; III. १३. १००; IV. 2. १११ and २४६; 4. ४१.

--a क्षेत्र and forest; a तीर्थ where Goddess लिन्गधारिणी is enshrined;
1: M. 1. 4; १३. २६.
best in कृतयुग;
2: Ib. १०६. ५७; १०९. 3; ११०. 1; १८०. ५५; २४६. ९३.
sacred to the पिट्र्स्; here the spokes of Haricakra (Dharmacakra- वा। प्।) fell to pieces; here is the image of विष्णु in वाराह form;
3: Ib. २२. १२, १४; वा. 1. १५.
the sage पिप्प्लाद living there was questioned by [page२-266+ ३०] युधिष्ठिर about अङ्गारकव्रत;
4: M. ७२, 2, Br. I. 2. 8; वा. 2. 8; २१. 1; २३. २०६; ७७. ९३; १०८. ४० and ४२.
the forest where the seers performed sacrifices.^5
